From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:22:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add the aarch64_ilp32 architecture

An ILP32 build of strace for AArch64 picked the aarch64 architecture,
which uses the 64-bit syscall table and does not link when long is
32 bits wide (the old time64 decoders are not built).

Detect __ILP32__ in configure and select a new single-personality
architecture, aarch64_ilp32, for ILP32 tracees: the generic 32-bit
syscall table (mmap2 with a 4096-byte offset unit, sync_file_range2),
32-bit kernel long, and the AArch64 general register set.  Syscall
arguments are the low halves of x0-x5; the result is a sign-extended
32-bit value in x0.

Add AUDIT_ARCH_AARCH64ILP32 to the audit_arch xlat, kernel headers
may not define it.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
